{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "conservative_regrid_assembly",
    "description": "Conservative-regridding assembly with weights computed INLINE from cell geometry (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §A.8 / §8.1; CONFORMANCE_SPEC.md §5.8; esm-spec.md §8.6.1; bead ess-my4.4.6). The source (F_src=[10,20,30,40]) is a SPATIALLY-VARYING field on a 4-cell source grid, remapped onto a DIFFERENT 4-cell target grid whose cell boundaries are shifted so the overlaps are fractional. Both grids tile [0,4]x[0,1] as in-file `const` vertex rings (src_poly / tgt_poly). The overlap weights are NOT supplied: A_ij = overlap_area_planar(src_i, tgt_j), the template of esm:std/geometry.esm, is declared inline, ranged over the bin-key candidate pairs; the candidate pairs come from the bin-key broad phase (floor → integer bin-key columns → distinct equi-join on the materialized bin buffers), A_j = Σ_i A_ij is the row-sum normalization, and W_ij = A_ij/A_j. F_tgt[j] = Σ_i W_ij·F_src[i] = [40/3, 20, 100/3, 40], conserving global mass Σ_j A_j·F_tgt = Σ_i A_i·F_src = 100 with partition-of-unity Σ_i W_ij = 1 by construction. Because the template returns the SCALAR overlap area (a convex clip and shoelace area written out in its body), A_ij is an ordinary DENSE faq over the candidate set with NO ragged intermediate. The dedicated Julia test geometry_assembly_conformance_test.jl drives the narrow phase (A_ij) plus apply/normalize (A_j, F_tgt, conservation, partition-of-unity) numerically from the in-file geometry.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST/polecats/gastown.nux"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "geometry",
      "conservative-regridding",
      "assembly",
      "overlap-join",
      "bin-key",
      "overlap_area_planar",
      "sum_product",
      "join",
      "filter",
      "inline-weights",
      "partition-of-unity",
      "conservation",
      "end-to-end",
      "ess-my4.4.6"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "coord": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    },
    "cell_verts": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "src_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "tgt_cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "candidate_pairs": {
      "kind": "derived",
      "from_faq": "candidate_set"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "ConservativeRegridAssembly": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "esm:std/relational.esm",
          "only": [
            "pair_key"
          ]
        },
        {
          "ref": "esm:std/geometry.esm",
          "only": [
            "overlap_area_planar"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "src_poly": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "cell_verts",
            "coord"
          ],
          "description": "In-file SOURCE-cell geometry: one closed lon-lat vertex ring per source cell (src_poly[i,v,1]=lon, src_poly[i,v,2]=lat), declared as a `const` array. The `poly_a` operand of the ranged narrow-phase clip. This is the cell geometry the overlap weights are computed FROM — nothing about the weights is supplied opaquely."
        },
        "tgt_poly": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells",
            "cell_verts",
            "coord"
          ],
          "description": "In-file TARGET-cell geometry: one closed lon-lat vertex ring per target cell — the `poly_b` operand of the ranged clip. The source and target grids tile the same domain [0,4]x[0,1] with DIFFERENT cell boundaries so the overlaps are fractional (the interesting regridding case)."
        },
        "src_lon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Source-cell representative longitude (bbox-min corner) — the float coord that enters ONLY the integer binning via `floor`, never a raw join comparison (§5.8.5)."
        },
        "src_lat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Source-cell representative latitude for binning."
        },
        "tgt_lon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Target-cell representative longitude for binning."
        },
        "tgt_lat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Target-cell representative latitude for binning."
        },
        "F_src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The SPATIALLY-VARYING source field being remapped (F_src=[10,20,30,40]). Non-uniform on purpose: a uniform field broadcast through the weights would be a no-op, so conservation and partition-of-unity are non-trivial."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Bin width in degrees — the integer quantization step of the broad phase (§5.8.5).",
          "default": 2.0
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Bin height in degrees.",
          "default": 2.0
        },
        "atol": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Sliver floor (§5.8.2): an overlap area at or below atol is treated as zero and dropped by the surviving-overlap filter.",
          "default": 1e-12
        },
        "pair_exists": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "candidate_pairs"
          ],
          "description": "Membership over the bin-key candidate overlap-pair set (the broad phase), materialized as the derived candidate_pairs index set via from_faq:\"candidate_set\"."
        },
        "A_ij": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "NARROW PHASE (densely evaluable): the overlap-area matrix A_ij[i,j] = the `overlap_area_planar` template of esm:std/geometry.esm applied to src_poly[i] and tgt_poly[j], computed INLINE from the in-file geometry. Ranged over the SAME bin-key candidate pairs (join.on [[src_bin,tgt_bin]]) as the row-sum / apply, so it is dense over the broad-phase candidate set with NO ragged intermediate: the template returns the SCALAR overlap area (its body clips one convex ring against the other and takes the shoelace area) with no intersection ring in the document. The weights are DECLARED from cell geometry in-file, not hand-supplied; the row-sum / apply halves below consume A_ij as the per-pair overlap-area factor."
        },
        "A_j": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Target-cell area denominator A_j[j] = Σ_i A_ij[i,j] — the group-by-`j` row-sum over the bin-key CANDIDATE pairs (join.on [[src_bin,tgt_bin]]) with the sub-atol sliver filter. The normalize denominator; = ConservativeRegridding.jl's `dst_areas`, here computed from geometry, not supplied."
        },
        "W_ij": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The conservative regrid weights W_ij = A_ij[i,j] / A_j[j] over the candidate pairs. Partition-of-unity Σ_i W_ij = 1 holds BY CONSTRUCTION because the denominator A_j is the row-sum of the SAME areas (§5.8.3)."
        },
        "A_j_check": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Tracer that recomputes A_j from the SAME A_ij feeding the apply (zero IC ⇒ du = A_j), the partition-of-unity-by-construction proof."
        },
        "F_tgt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "The regridded field F_tgt[j] = Σ_i W_ij[i,j]·F_src[i] = (1/A_j[j])·Σ_i A_ij[i,j]·F_src[i] — the apply sum_product FAQ over the candidate set. Zero IC ⇒ du = F_tgt. Conservation Σ_j A_j·F_tgt[j] = Σ_i A_i·F_src[i] and PoU Σ_i W_ij = 1 hold."
        },
        "src_bin_c1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Component 1 of the key formerly `src_bin` (an integer join column)."
        },
        "src_bin_c2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Component 2 of the key formerly `src_bin` (an integer join column)."
        },
        "tgt_bin_c1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Component 1 of the key formerly `tgt_bin` (an integer join column)."
        },
        "tgt_bin_c2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "tgt_cells"
          ],
          "description": "Component 2 of the key formerly `tgt_bin` (an integer join column)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "Component 1 of the former `skolem` key `src_bin`: an integer join column.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "index",
            "args": [
              "src_bin_c1",
              "i"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "src_cells"
              }
            },
            "args": [],
            "expr": {
              "op": "floor",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "/",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "src_lon",
                        "i"
                      ]
                    },
                    "dx"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "Component 2 of the former `skolem` key `src_bin`: an integer join column.",
